    "localmaxxing": {
      "hardware_label": "GB10 Grace Blackwell",
      "notes": "Single-stream decode, batch 1, one concurrent request. n=9 generations (3 prompt kinds x 3 repeats), 512 output tokens each, streaming, temperature 0.6 / top_p 0.95 / top_k 20. Context length 131072 is the CONFIGURED window, not the prompt depth; prompts here are short. mem-fraction-static 0.80, kv-cache-dtype fp8_e4m3, attention backend flashinfer, tp 1, max-running-requests 32. Idle box, one model loaded at a time, and all 6 cells of this battery ran back to back in one session on one machine. SPECULATIVE DECODING OFF, no draft model loaded. This is the no-draft baseline arm of a DFlash2 comparison, so it is deliberately low and should not be read as this stack's practical speed. Per-workload decode: code 10.97, reasoning 10.97, prose 10.99 tok/s; the headline is the mean of all 9. Spread across workloads is under 0.03 tok/s, which is what a decode path with no draft looks like. Quantization detail: Unsloth Dynamic V3.0 compressed-tensors mixed precision, MLP gate/up/down NVFP4 W4A4 group 16, attention and layers 56-63 MLP FP8, lm_head FP8 per-channel, MTP head BF16 unquantised. Served from a local copy, so the Hugging Face revision was not recorded; the checkpoint is pinned instead by its config.json sha256 1b3c71868d1299e52df6fc907deb202d5132b1ef0f72aae0ef6d15185dd53a5c. TTFT is the mean of the same 9 runs.",
